dialect protocol stdio.step.snapshot
; `StepSnapshot::encode_pack_with` is: a `SemioEnvelope` header (`wrap_binary`, envelope id
; `stdio.step`, component `Pack`, version 1) followed by the UTF-8 bytes of the SAME Part-21 text
; the DSL facet emits (`write_part21(&self.to_part21_document())`) — no separate packed binary
; layout exists at this facet; the pack form is envelope-framed text, documented here rather than
; hidden behind a placeholder. See the sibling text grammar
; (`../📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`) for `exchange-file`'s own definition.
root = pack-payload
pack-payload = semio-envelope exchange-file-bytes
semio-envelope = envelope-id component-tag version-tag
envelope-id = 'stdio.step'
component-tag = 'pack'
version-tag = '1'
exchange-file-bytes = utf8-bytes-of(exchange-file) ; `exchange-file` per the sibling text grammar
